WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.000
What if there’s only one landmark in sight?

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.750
One lighthouse on an empty coast.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.025
One bearing gives you one line, and one line isn’t a fix.

4
00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:12.250
The answer is clever.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.800
Use the same landmark twice.

6
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.950
That’s a running fix.

7
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.025
Look at the diagram.

8
00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:22.325
Take a bearing, and plot the line of position.

9
00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:25.450
Keep going, on a steady course and speed.

10
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.075
Later, take a second bearing.

11
00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:30.550
Now advance the first line.

12
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:37.400
Slide it, parallel to itself, in the direction of your course, by the distance you ran between the bearings.

13
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.025
Where the advanced line crosses the second line is your running fix.

14
00:00:43.025 --> 00:00:44.750
What’s the weak point?

15
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.750
It depends on your course and speed over the ground being what you think they are.

16
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.575
If an unknown current is pushing you between the two bearings, the running fix will be off.
